    {
      "by": "adhami3310",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-01T23:53:25Z",
      "excerpt": "The revert is deliberate: rather than rewording around it, the renderer bug is fixed at its source in #7383, which keeps inline code inside link text. These links render as written once that merges, and the same fix covers the pages on main that already use this pattern. _🤖 Addressed by [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "at": "2026-10-02T00:57:02Z",
      "excerpt": "**Wake can return mid-step** When a worker starts a long-running step, its next pass can find nothing else to claim and make `wake()` return `True` while that step is still running. On a host that suspends after a successful wake response, this newly documented guarantee can cause the host to suspend mid-step. The API reference repeats the same guarantee."
    },
    {
      "by": "adhami3310",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-02T00:57:20Z",
      "excerpt": "Right about current main: that is the bug fixed in #7385, where a pass only counts as settled when no step is in flight, so wake() no longer returns True mid-step. These docs describe that behavior, so #7385 should merge before or with this PR. _🤖 Addressed by [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "at": "2026-10-02T00:57:42Z",
      "excerpt": "P2: `wake` does not wait for the steps it started to finish in the current runner, so this sentence is inaccurate. `Runner.loop` records a settled pass whenever a pass claims nothing, which also happens while steps are still in flight once `max_concurrency` is saturated (free becomes 0, so `started` stays 0), and `Settled.after` then returns `True`. The commit notes this matches #7385, but that runner change is not in this checkout. Either drop \"every step it started has finished\" to match curre"
    },
    {
      "by": "cubic-dev-ai",
      "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "at": "2026-10-02T00:57:42Z",
      "excerpt": "**All reported issues were addressed** across 2 files (changes from recent commits). **Tip**: Review your code locally with the [cubic CLI](https://docs.cubic.dev/ide/cli-review?utm_source=github&utm_content=general_review_body) to iterate faster. [Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/reflex-dev/reflex/7379/ai_pr_review_github_delivery_3e813784eae3951303f379472318b307101e5b7c55d820d5f29cdb08e9ea9e0b?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Freflex-dev%2Freflex%2Fpull%2F7379)"
    },
    {
      "by": "adhami3310",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-02T01:01:06Z",
      "excerpt": "Not changed here: this sentence describes the behavior in #7385, which records a settled pass only when no step is in flight (the saturated-concurrency case included, since those steps are in flight). Your second point was valid there too: #7385 now also skips a pass during which the wake event was set, with a test that starts a run in that gap. #7385 should merge before or with this PR. _🤖 Addressed by [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)_"
    }
  ],
